cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this proof, harness or the findings, please cite it as below."
title: "hazard3-formal: formal equivalence of Hazard3 and the RISC-V Sail model"
authors:
  - family-names: Strijbos
    given-names: Leo
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-20
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/leostrijbos/hazard3-formal"
abstract: >-
  An unbounded proof, with open-source tools, that an RV32IMC + Zicsr
  machine-mode configuration of Hazard3 v1.1.1 (the RISC-V core in the
  Raspberry Pi RP2350) is trace equivalent to the RISC-V Sail specification,
  modulo one stated axiom (the multiplier/divider arithmetic), together with
  the five Hazard3 and one Sail-model divergences the proof found.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - RISC-V
  - Hazard3
  - Sail
  - k-induction
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Ibex formal verification against the Sail model (ibex/dv/formal)"
    authors:
      - name: "lowRISC contributors"
      - family-names: Ploix
        given-names: Louis-Emile
    repository-code: "https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex"
    license: Apache-2.0
  - type: software
    title: "Hazard3"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wren
        given-names: Luke
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Wren6991/Hazard3"
    version: 1.1.1
    license: Apache-2.0
